  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nAn upper ridge over the western states will bring the heat back to\nthe area through the weekend. A weak frontal system will help to\nbring west winds today.\n\nAbundant smoke from the Pacific NW fires will move into the\nforecast area today with reduced visibility. Will mention haze in\nthe forecast to account for this. \n\nWest winds will be strong enough this afternoon for a Lake Wind \nAdvisory.\n\nWill expand the Extreme Heat Warning to include all areas. It \nlooks like Saturday will be the hottest day with highs above 100 \nin most areas and a few locations like Glendive and Terry above \n105 for highs. Heat impact level maps are recommending an Extreme\nHeat Warning for all areas on Saturday. To keep the headlines\nsimple, will include all areas today through Sunday in the\nwarning. Flow aloft turns SW Saturday afternoon and evening while\na shortwave trough and weak cold front brings a chance for \nshowers and thunderstorms Saturday evening. Highs on Sunday will \nonly be a few degrees cooler with highs near 100. \n\nWill maintain Red Flag Warning for today. Will not include  \nSaturday for now as winds are expected to be light. Fire weather \nissues may arise Sunday with higher winds and low humidity. \nHowever zones 136 and 137 may not have the wind to reach the \ncriteria.\n\nThe upper ridge next week tries to push east but an upper trough \nover the eastern US keeps it at bay. Expect a slight cooldown but\ntemps will remain above normal with mainly dry conditions.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nLow confidence that there will be a thunderstorm somewhere in \nnortheast Montana tonight, based on HREF. High confidence on \nbreezy west winds on Friday and on the heat this weekend.",
